# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets serves files by extension, ignoring
# whatever Content-Type an Astro endpoint (llms.txt.ts, [slug].md.ts) set
# on its Response at build time — confirmed live: both shipped as
# text/plain and text/markdown respectively, with no charset parameter,
# which mis-renders em-dashes and other non-ASCII characters for anyone
# opening the raw file directly in a browser. This file (the same
# mechanism Cloudflare Pages uses) is the only way to attach a real
# charset to a static asset response.
/llms.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

/*/*.md
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
